  "$comment": "Figma parity manifest (MASTER-PLAN §3, manifest split C3). Keyed by ref id from the design-refs repo's refs.json; holds what lives with the code: the Storybook target, probe selectors (relative to target.root; ':scope' is the root itself), tolerance overrides and waivers. A token probe's optional cssVar is the CSS expression behind a Figma variable whose name is not one (P3); probe 1's sentinel check overrides the custom properties it names. `@theme inline` inlines a theme variable into its utility (rounded-md compiles to calc(var(--radius) - 2px), not var(--radius-md)), so cssVar must name what the compiled CSS references. Run: node scripts/vrt/vrt.mjs parity --refs <local refs checkout> --out <dir>. Until O4 creates the refs repo, scripts/ci/tests/fixtures/parity is the local stand-in for these ids. Report-only in slice 1.0b.",
